"""
check_nextcloud - LibreNMS/Nagios service check for a Nextcloud server

Language: -l zh-tw|en (default zh-tw).

One plugin, one aspect per service (-C):
    status    status.php: installed, maintenance mode, pending DB upgrade
              (no login needed)
    updates   Nextcloud core and app updates
    storage   free space of the data directory, users, files
    shares    share counts, public links without a password
    users     active users (5 min / 1 h / 24 h / 7 days)
    php       OPcache (enabled, full, hit rate, wasted memory, interned
              strings) and APCu memory
    system    load per CPU and memory of the Nextcloud host
    database  database type, version and size
    setup     the admin overview's setup checks (cron last run, missing
              indices, security warnings, log errors ...); cached

Everything except status reads the serverinfo API
(/ocs/v2.php/apps/serverinfo/api/v1/info) and needs an admin account, or a
serverinfo token (--nc-token). setup needs an admin account.

Replaces check_nextcloud.py (BornToBeRoot), whose "apps" check crashes on
Nextcloud 28+ because serverinfo skips the app list unless asked for it.

Version: 1.0
Author: Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>
https://github.com/jasoncheng7115/jt-lnms-plugins
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later

LibreNMS invokes this as:
    <nagios_plugins>/check_nextcloud -H <service_ip|hostname> <service_param>

Usage:
    check_nextcloud -H cloud.example.com -C status|updates|storage|shares|
                    users|php|system|database|setup
                    [-P 443] [--http] [-k] [-u USER] [-a AUTH_FILE]
                    [--password PASS] [--nc-token TOKEN] [-t 30] [-l zh-tw|en]

Credentials, in order of precedence: --password, --auth-file (one line
"user:password", readable only by the LibreNMS user), environment variable
NEXTCLOUD_PASSWORD. Prefer --auth-file: service parameters are shown in the
LibreNMS web UI and in the process list.

Exit: 0 OK / 1 WARNING / 2 CRITICAL / 3 UNKNOWN
"""

